  "comment": "**What it does**\nSolid income REITs \u2014 a fat but sustainable payout, filling the type the other screens exclude.\n- **Your choices:** 4-10% yield (REITs are legally high payers), revenue not shrinking, leverage within REIT norms, $1B+, moderate risk.\n- Debt tests carry `is null` fallbacks so a REIT is never dropped merely for missing a debt figure, exactly as the brief asked.\n\n**How to tweak**\n- Widen it: lower the `market_cap` floor from $1B, or the yield band's bottom from 4%.\n- Safer only: raise `interest_coverage` from 1.5 to 2.5.\n- The REIT universe is small (~291 rows), so counts here will always be modest.\n\n**How to sort for best picks**\n- Sort by `income_score`, tiebreak `quality_score`.\n- Avoid sorting by `growth_score` (REITs are income vehicles) and raw `div_yield_ttm` for the same yield-trap reason as above.\n\n_Built 2026-08-13 \u00b7 31 matches at build time._",
  "ai_instructions": "Find solid income REITs \u2014 real-estate trusts with a fat but sustainable payout.\nThis fills the type my other screens exclude.\n- **Goal**: income. **Kinds**: REITs only. **Dividends**: required.\n- **Yield**: roughly 4-10% (REITs are legally high payers; above ~10% smells like\n  trouble).\n- **Still growing**: revenue should not be shrinking.\n- **Debt in check**: leverage within normal REIT norms, interest comfortably paid;\n  never drop a REIT just because a debt metric has no data.\n- **Size**: $1B and bigger. **Risk**: moderate. **Results**: ~30-150 names.\n- **Sorting**: income first, tiebreak quality.",
